Drop a corporate root CA here, as a PEM-encoded .crt file, if your network inspects TLS.

Every image build that reaches the network - dotnet restore, npm ci - copies this folder into the container's
trust store before it starts. On a normal network the folder is empty and nothing changes; behind an
intercepting proxy an empty folder means restore fails with "the remote certificate is invalid because of
errors in the certificate chain", which looks like a broken Dockerfile and is a missing CA.

Export one on Windows:

  $cert = Get-ChildItem Cert:\LocalMachine\Root | Where-Object { $_.Subject -match 'Zscaler' } | Select-Object -First 1
  $pem = "-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----`n" + [Convert]::ToBase64String($cert.RawData, 'InsertLineBreaks') + "`n-----END CERTIFICATE-----"
  Set-Content -Path certs/corporate-root.crt -Value $pem -Encoding ascii

Contents are gitignored: a CA is specific to one network and has no business in this repository.
